    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n24165" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">intĕr-āresco</span></b> ,
			ĕre, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>v. inch. n.</i>, <i>to become
			dry</i>, <i>to dry up.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <i><span class="en">Vitr. 7, 8,
				2</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">animalia sine humoris potestate interarescent,</span>”
				<i>will die off</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					8 praef.</span></i>
			 § 3.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, <i>to dry up</i>, <i>decay;</i> with exstingui et cadere, <i><span class="en">Cic. Tusc.
				5, 14, 40</span></i>.</div>
